  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Kingdom&#x2019;s Resettlement Scheme (UKRS) and the Mandate Scheme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports the resettlement of up to 3,000 of the world&#x2019;s most vulnerable refugees meeting one of UNHCR&apos;s seven resettlement submission categories. Local Authority capacity is also taken into account to ensure that the type of cases referred can be resettled in the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland (UK). IOM is facilitating video/telephone interviewing, provision of pre-migration health activities and facilitating the early identification of adult beneficiaries&#x2019; mental health needs and children&#x2019;s Special Educational Needs (SEN) through the application of the Global Mental Health Assessment Tool (GMHAT) and targeted SEN questions in specific departure Missions, pre-embarkation checks, three-day pre-departure orientation (UKCO) sessions, visa/travel document processing, and movement management and operational support to the final destination including operational and/or medical escorts and the delivery of information sessions to Local Authority, community sponsors, and other relevant resettlement stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
